    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d903">

                <pb facs="0952" n="940" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg940"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 Roszkowski, Mieczyslaw/14:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-28T13:00:00+03:00">February 28,
                            1941—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 28—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>388. My 275, February 13, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d903-f1"/> The Embassy is in receipt of a note from the Commissariat
                    for Foreign Affairs to the effect that the “Mechislav Ignatevich Rozhkovski, who
                    was born in 1920, has been sentenced by the public court of Lapski <hi
                        rendition="#italic">raion</hi> to 3 years of reformatory labor camp for
                    unlawful keeping of arms.[”] The note further states that Rozhkovski “has a
                    birth certificate attested to by the city clerk at the city of Fall River,
                    Massachusetts, United States of America” but no other documents to confirm his
                    American citizenship.</p>
                <p>I am addressing a further note to the Commissariat for Foreign Affairs
                    reasserting Rozhkovski’s American citizenship and requesting permission for a
                    representative of the Embassy to interview him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
